WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:20.000
EPA 608 is not optional. You cannot legally touch refrigerant without it. Let's
make sure you pass.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:40.000
DOT (Department of Transportation) regulates refrigerant cylinders. Every
cylinder has a DOT specification stamped on the collar: the spec number, working
pressure, water capacity, tare weight, and hydrostatic test date. Cylinders must

00:00:40.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Here are the key terms. Write these down.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:20.000
Hydrostatic Test Date: Stamped on the cylinder collar. Must be within 5 years or
the cylinder cannot be refilled.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:40.000
Tare Weight: The empty weight of the cylinder. Used to calculate how much
refrigerant is inside.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Water Capacity: The total volume of the cylinder. Never fill above 80% of this
value.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:20.000
Here's why this matters on the job: Check the hydrostatic test date before every
recovery job. An expired cylinder at a supply house is a red flag — do not use
it.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:40.000
Watch out for these: Gray body, yellow top = DOT recovery cylinder color
standard. And — Never refill a disposable cylinder — it is a federal violation

00:02:40.000 --> 00:03:00.000
Quick check: what is the maximum fine for knowingly venting refrigerant? If you
don't know that number, go back and read it again.

